#: ../../source/buffer-from_readme.md:1
msgid "Buffer From"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/buffer-from_readme.md:3
msgid ""
"A [ponyfill](https://ponyfill.com) for `Buffer.from`, uses native "
"implementation if available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/buffer-from_readme.md:5
msgid "Installation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/buffer-from_readme.md:11
msgid "Usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/buffer-from_readme.md:31
msgid "API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/buffer-from_readme.md:33
msgid "bufferFrom(array)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/buffer-from_readme.md:35
msgid "`array` &lt;Array&gt;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/buffer-from_readme.md:37
msgid "Allocates a new `Buffer` using an `array` of octets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/buffer-from_readme.md:39
msgid "bufferFrom(arrayBuffer[, byteOffset[, length]])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/buffer-from_readme.md:41
msgid ""
"`arrayBuffer` &lt;ArrayBuffer&gt; The `.buffer` property of a TypedArray "
"or ArrayBuffer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/buffer-from_readme.md:42
msgid ""
"`byteOffset` &lt;Integer&gt; Where to start copying from `arrayBuffer`. "
"**Default:** `0`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/buffer-from_readme.md:43
msgid ""
"`length` &lt;Integer&gt; How many bytes to copy from `arrayBuffer`. "
"**Default:** `arrayBuffer.length - byteOffset`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/buffer-from_readme.md:45
msgid ""
"When passed a reference to the `.buffer` property of a TypedArray "
"instance, the newly created `Buffer` will share the same allocated memory"
" as the TypedArray."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/buffer-from_readme.md:48
msgid ""
"The optional `byteOffset` and `length` arguments specify a memory range "
"within the `arrayBuffer` that will be shared by the `Buffer`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/buffer-from_readme.md:51
msgid "bufferFrom(buffer)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/buffer-from_readme.md:53
msgid "`buffer` &lt;Buffer&gt; An existing `Buffer` to copy data from"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/buffer-from_readme.md:55
msgid "Copies the passed `buffer` data onto a new `Buffer` instance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/buffer-from_readme.md:57
msgid "bufferFrom(string[, encoding])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/buffer-from_readme.md:59
msgid "`string` &lt;String&gt; A string to encode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/buffer-from_readme.md:60
msgid "`encoding` &lt;String&gt; The encoding of `string`. **Default:** `'utf8'`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/buffer-from_readme.md:62
msgid ""
"Creates a new `Buffer` containing the given JavaScript string `string`. "
"If provided, the `encoding` parameter identifies the character encoding "
"of `string`."
msgstr ""

